			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add PostHog environment variable defines to ESBuild config\n\nAdd PostHogDefines to TargetConfig.ts that maps LAND_POSTHOG_* environment\nvariables to esbuild define directives. This enables the browser bundle to\naccess PostHog configuration (key, host, enabled flags, session recording,\nsurveys, distinct_id) at build time through import.meta.env.*.\n\nThe esbuild define directive is required because Wind's PostHog consumer\nprefers import.meta.env over process.env, but browser contexts lack the\nlatter. This completes the work from the recent commit that removed the\nhardcoded API key, enabling PostHog configuration to be driven entirely by\nenvironment variables while preserving sensible defaults.",
			"SHA": "bb3b6fc39e98bda69fb8d639f8e125150f1f9ce9"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T21:13:05Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1049,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Wind): Remove hardcoded PostHog API key from configuration\n\nReplace the hardcoded PostHog API key in Configuration.ts with an empty string. Hardcoded API keys should never be committed to version control as they could be accidentally exposed or misused.\n\nThis ensures the default configuration doesn't include credentials that could leak in public commits.",
			"SHA": "a0e09d67d163ccd6ea9720de1d5a5d47ce2715c0"
